exports[`tool surface as a client sees it > allow list / all apps 1`] = `
{
  "count": 2,
  "instructions": "This server's policy denies edit and destroy tools by default, so some write tools are not registered. TeamDynamix ticketing and assets. Workflow: search/get/create/update directly. app_id accepts an application name ('Help Desk') or ID, and status, priority, type and similar arguments accept names ('On Hold') or IDs; a wrong name returns the valid choices. Search tools return partial records; call the matching get tool for full detail. Page with limit/offset or the next_cursor returned in each response; a total shown as 'N+' is a lower bound. Use count_only=true for 'how many' questions and verbosity='compact' when scanning many records. Person arguments accept an email address or 'me' (the signed-in user under SSO) as well as a UID, so a lookup call is usually unnecessary. Pass response_format='json' when you need structured data instead of prose. For large or cross-entity questions prefer tdx_get_report and tdx_run_saved_search. To record progress on a ticket use tdx_add_ticket_comment; tdx_edit_ticket rewrites core fields and may be disabled. Tools annotated readOnlyHint:false change TeamDynamix records; obtain user approval before invoking them.",
  "prompts": [],
  "tools": [
    "tdx_get_ticket",
    "tdx_search_assets",
  ],
}
`;

